\label{prop:conjcsh}
Suppose that $T$ is an IET of hyperbolic periodic type. Let $\omega_1,\omega_2\in{\mathbb{R}}^{\mathcal A}$ be log-slope vectors of central-stable type such that their difference $\omega:=\omega_1-\omega_2$ is of stable type. Let $f_1$, $f_2$ be two AIETs such that $f_1\in \operatorname{Aff}(T,\omega_1)$ and $f_2\in \operatorname{Aff}(T,\omega_2)$. Then the conjugacy $h$ between $f_1$ and $f_2$ is such that
\[\mathfrak{H}(h), \mathfrak{H}(h^{-1})\geq 1+\frac{\alpha(\omega)}{\zeta^{f_1}}.\]
